<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/
..\FrameXML\UI.xsd">

    <!-- Vendored, not `externals:` in `.pkgmeta`. An external is only fetched by the packager, so
         the working tree would not have these files and neither the headless specs (`tests/run.js`
         loads real source under fengari) nor a locally-copied build would see them.

         LibStub is not loaded here. Debind loads it and Debind is a hard dependency, so it is
         already up by the time this addon is opened. Loading a second copy would be harmless but
         it would also be the only reason this addon needed Debind's Libs folder at all. -->
    <Script file="Libs\LibDeflate\LibDeflate.lua"/>

    <!-- **LibSerialize is pinned to v1.2.1 (MINOR 5).** Not because anything is wrong with
         v1.2.2 - because of the client we develop against.

         v1.2.2's negative-zero check opens with `if num == 0 and 1 / num < 0`, which is correct
         under IEEE 754 and answers `inf` on every runtime that follows it: retail, desktop Lua
         5.1, desktop 5.4. The `_ptr_` client here is an older build that raises "Division by
         zero" on that instead, and every payload we build is full of zeros (`spec = 0` on each
         account-wide layer, a random-favourite mount, any zeroed condition mask). So on that one
         client v1.2.2 cannot export at all, and that client is where this gets tested.

         Nothing to report upstream and nothing for us to work around. Take v1.2.2 whenever the
         PTR install catches up. `.zzz/export-import.md` has the measurements. -->
    <Script file="Libs\LibSerialize\LibSerialize.lua"/>

</Ui>
